From: JiaY-shi <shi05275@163.com>
Date: Thu, 30 Jul 2026 17:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] block: skip NAND mtdblock devices attached to UBI

The block utility keeps probing rootfs and rootfs_data on NAND for
compatibility with devices using JFFS2 or SquashFS directly on MTD.
This also probes the raw mtdblock device when the partition is already
attached to UBI, producing repeated mtdblock warnings during boot.

An attached UBI device is visible below the MTD sysfs directory.  Skip
the raw block device in that case while preserving the compatibility
probe for NAND partitions which are not managed by UBI.

Signed-off-by: JiaY-shi <shi05275@163.com>
---
 block.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

--- a/block.c
+++ b/block.c
@@ -490,6 +490,7 @@ static bool mtdblock_is_nand(char *mtdnu
 {
 	char tmppath[64];
 	char buf[16];
+	glob_t gl;
 	FILE *fp;
 
 	snprintf(tmppath, sizeof(tmppath) - 1, "/sys/class/mtd/mtd%s/type", mtdnum);
@@ -508,6 +509,14 @@ static bool mtdblock_is_nand(char *mtdnu
 	if (strcmp(buf, "nand"))
 		return false;
 
+	/* UBI owns this MTD, so probing its raw block device is redundant. */
+	snprintf(tmppath, sizeof(tmppath) - 1,
+		 "/sys/class/mtd/mtd%s/ubi[0-9]*", mtdnum);
+	if (!glob(tmppath, GLOB_NOSORT, NULL, &gl)) {
+		globfree(&gl);
+		return true;
+	}
+
 	/*
 	 * --- CUT HERE ---
 	 * Keep probing rootfs and rootfs_data in the meantime to not break
